Adapted from TextFold, with changes, for Obsidian:
- the five reading levels (Full, Key, Brief, Takeaway, Topic) and the split between the
  author's words and a model's (textfold/ladder.py, docs/format.md);
- the prompts that write the levels and the sentence-aligned translations
  (textfold/ladder.py, textfold/translate.py), extended to write the short levels in two
  languages at once;
- the local fold of a text by its first sentences (plugins/textfold/hooks/fold.ts);
- the question prompt that cites paragraphs by number (textfold/notes.py).
The code is a new TypeScript implementation; the Markdown parser, the Obsidian views, the
translation views, the chat and the model clients are new.

It bundles the Anthropic TypeScript SDK (@anthropic-ai/sdk, MIT License).
